# philosophy.entoolment-is-the-pinnacle.via-routes

> a route IS a 🔩 rigid skill: deterministic entrypoint, mixed operations + orchestration.

deterministic: stones, order, guards, passage ledger, review judge (they refuse, order, and tally identically). probabilistic: the work at each stone. the deterministic half drives the brain — it cannot pass by decision, never recalls what is next, and is pulled back to the road.

| the leftover work is… | pave as… |
|---|---|
| a step, same every time | 🪨 solid skill |
| a sequence of commands | 💧 or 🔩 skill |
| judgment at several points, order matters | 🔩 a route |

do not route what could be entooled: a route around deterministic work charges imagine cost at every stone.

🗿 offroad work earns its keep by what it paves: end it with a route left behind.
